          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying an Expensive Machine and a Cheap Grinder</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The grinder sets the ceiling on shot quality. Spending most of the budget on the machine and pairing it with a blade grinder or pre-ground coffee wastes what the machine can do. Balance the budget, or choose a grinder-built-in model.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using Stale Supermarket Coffee</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Espresso exaggerates staleness. Beans more than a few weeks past their roast date, or pre-ground coffee, produce thin, sour shots on any machine. Buy beans with a roast date and grind just before brewing.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping Descaling</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Scale builds silently inside boilers and thermoblocks until flow drops or heaters fail. Follow the manual's descaling schedule for your water hardness, and use filtered water to stretch the interval.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring Counter Space and Height</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Machines with bean hoppers and grinders can be taller than expected and may not fit under wall cabinets. Measure the space, including room to fill the water tank and hopper, before buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting Café Results on Day One</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Manual machines take practice. Expect to adjust grind, dose and timing over the first few weeks. A scale and a timer shorten the learning curve far more than upgrading hardware.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

